          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ഞരങ്ങുക — ñaraṅṅuka — \"to groan; to moan\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "വേദന കാരണം രോഗി രാത്രി മുഴുവൻ ഞരങ്ങി. vēdana kāraṇaṁ rōgi rātri muḻuvan ñaraṅṅi. The patient groaned all night because of the pain."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past: ഞരങ്ങി, ñaraṅṅi."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A low sound of pain; the noun is ഞരക്കം."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ഞരങ്ങുക (ñaraṅṅuka) is native Dravidian: DEDR 2904 gives the Malayalam verb as to grumble or groan, with ഞരക്കം, a moan (DEDR 2904)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
