          "title": "You'll want to know: പരിഭവം",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "പരിഭവം — paribhavaṁ — \"a hurt feeling; a mild grievance\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "പിറന്നാളിന് വിളിക്കാത്തതിൽ സുഹൃത്തിന് പരിഭവം ഉണ്ട്. piṟannāḷinŭ viḷikkāttatil suhṛttinŭ paribhavaṁ uṇṭŭ. My friend is hurt that I didn't call on his birthday."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A soft, hurt complaint between people close to each other, milder than ദേഷ്യം."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "പരിഭവം (paribhavaṁ) is borrowed from Sanskrit paribhava, \"an insult, a humiliation\" (Monier-Williams). In Malayalam it softened into the hurt one feels at being slighted."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
